  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Potassium iodide is used as an expectorant for coughs, as an ophthalmological preparation, and as an antidote, and is listed among WHO essential medicines. It is an approved medicine used in various settings, though it carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q121874&quot;>Wikidata Q121874</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>potassium iodide</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>R05CA02, S01XA04, V03AB21</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB06715&quot;>DB06715</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4875&quot;>4875</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:8346&quot;>8346</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q121874&quot;>Q121874</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>IK</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>165.998 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
